    "body": "More evidence from the maintainer, from chat on 2026-11-22. The screenshot shows the Heights tab of the same operation, `2D Offset1`. It is not attached here.\n\nHeights tab:\n- Clearance Z: from \"Top of stock\", offset 10.0 mm, so Z 32.000.\n- Top Z: from \"Top of stock\", offset 0.0 mm, so Z 22.000.\n- Bottom Z: from \"Selection\", offset 1.5 mm, so Z 1.500.\n- Levels: \"Hop below clearance\" is off. Stepdown is 10.0 mm.\n\nThe status line of this run reads `OK - 1764 moves - 2 warnings`:\n1. `move 522 cuts past the finish surface - repeated on 62 more moves (to 1710)`.\n2. `rapid move 543 travels through stock (below the clearance plane, or at it below the stock top) - repeated on 2 more moves (to 1711)`.\n\nWhat this shows:\n- Every height is above the stock top (Z 22.000). The clearance plane is not inside the stock. So warning 2 does not come from a low plane.\n- \"Hop below clearance\" is off. The rapids must then ride at the clearance plane. Three lateral rapids (moves 543 to 1711) are below it and cross uncut stock. They break the setting. The maintainer asked why.\n- Warning 1 is a cut into the finish surface from move 522. Warning 2 starts 21 moves later. They may share the cause of this issue: passes that start inside the containment and work outward, with a link that the generator treats as air.\n\nThe worker checks if warnings 1 and 2 have the same cause as the slotting. If the cause differs, the worker files a separate issue for the three rapids and names it here. Use `fig8.step` and `EM-0800-4FL` with these heights (Clearance +10, Top +0, Bottom +1.5 from the selection, Stepdown 10, Hop below clearance off).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
