    "body": "Answer from the code to the question of #3318: which height does a \"Retract plane\" pass link of a 2D Offset use when \"Hop below clearance\" is off?\n\n- With hop off, the operation stores `retract_z: None`.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` passes `hl.retract` (None) into `PocketParams::retract_z`.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/levels.rs:179` sets `hop_z: retract_z.unwrap_or(clearance_z).min(clearance_z)`.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/ladder_links.rs` (`pass_link`, `level_link`) uses `m.hop_z` for `Link::Retract`.\n\nResult: the \"Retract plane\" link lifts to Clearance Z (Z 32.000 in the maintainer's operation). This agrees with the Heights hint \"off: every link climbs to Clearance Z\". The 2D Offset generator has no hidden retract height at \"stock top +10\". If `operations-2d.md` says that, the document is wrong for this case (#3318).\n\nThus the three lateral rapids below Z 32 (moves 543 to 1711) are not retract-plane links. I will find their source from the move list of the pin run and report it here.",
