    "body": "Escalation from issue-worker-high: the review fix of PR #3353 is larger than `effort:high`. I raise the label to `effort:max` and release the claim.\n\nWhat I learned (I agree with the second read, comment 7077845657):\n- The rank of `PassStart::rank` orders closed rings by winding. After a ring splits, each piece is one closed counter-clockwise loop. That loop has arcs at offset k from the outer boundary (stock side) AND arcs at offset k from the hole (part side). The part-side arcs wrap around the part where the band is wide. On those arcs the material on both sides is uncut, so the tool cuts at full width.\n- No order of closed rings removes this. One piece loop needs its stock-side arcs cut early and its part-side arcs cut late. So a rank of whole loops cannot be correct after a split.\n\nWhat a correct Outside needs (new ring geometry, not a new order):\n- Level curves of the distance from the start boundary only: ring j is the boundary of the outer region (holes filled) offset by `-j * stepover`, clipped to the cutter-center area. The clipped parts are OPEN paths that end on the hole boundary.\n- Cut ring j before ring j + 1. Then the hole wall ring (offset 0) last. Inside is the mirror (holes dilated by `j * stepover`, the outer wall ring last).\n- Each open path is its own pass, or a chain where a chord is proved. Keep-down links need a new proof: a chord between two open path ends can run through uncut material near the wall.\n- The geometry crate has no open-path clip against a `Region` today (searched: no such function). It must be written and tested (Clipper2 supports open subjects).\n- The start-side wall cases (Outside on a closed pocket, Inside on an Outside band or on an island) start with a wall ring at full width. They need a visible note on the toolpath. The app layer knows the containment, so it can name the case.\n\nState of the work:\n- PR #3353 (draft, head 59b42c727) is unchanged. Its texts \"no ring is a full slot\" (rank doc comment, `docs/decisions/3316-pass-start-shared.md`, hint in `pass_start_row.rs`, MCP skill row, `Changelog:` line) are not true after a split. The next worker must correct them.\n- The type, the field, the project key, the MCP door, the UI row and the pins of #3353 stay useful. Only the ring law in `waterscan.rs` / `pass_start.rs` needs the new geometry.\n- The pin `fig8_outside_offset_starts_each_level_at_the_stock_edge` checks only the first and the last move of each level. The next worker adds the engagement check along the whole level (the reviewer's 100 x 40 / radius 15 case in motion, and fig8 in app), red first.\n- No new code was written in this run. The worktree `.claude/worktrees/issue-3316` holds only the pushed head.\n",
